Terrain (Copernicus DEM licence, modified data):
produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 (c) DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018
provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved

Precipitation: CHELSA V2.1 bio12 (1981-2010), CC0 1.0. Karger, D.N., Conrad, O., Böhner, J., Kawohl, T., Kreft, H.,
Soria-Auza, R.W., Zimmermann, N.E., Linder, H.P. & Kessler, M. (2021) Climatologies at high resolution for the earth's
land surface areas. EnviDat. https://doi.org/10.16904/envidat.228.v2.1 ; Karger et al. (2017) Scientific Data 4, 170122.

Rain-gauge data: Israel Meteorological Service, meteorological data archive, data.gov.il dataset 481
(https://data.gov.il/dataset/481), licence "Other (Open)" as stated on the dataset.

Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0): many facts in content/ cite English and Hebrew Wikipedia articles, and the 1948 settlement
coordinates come from the Wikipedia API; each entry lists its source URLs.

Sub-district boundaries (content/map/subdistricts_1948.geojson): digitised from the Survey of Palestine map
"Administrative Divisions" (1946, overprinted May 1947) and the Administrative Divisions (Amendment) Proclamation, 1947
(Palestine Gazette No. 1552), Government of Palestine works (public domain in Israel and the UK; facts only are used: decision D-B in
docs/oss/DECISIONS.md; see the file's licence note); scans from
the National Library of Israel via Wikimedia Commons. Hebrew and Arabic names from Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).

Railways and roads of 1948 (content/map/route*_1948.yaml): traced on the Survey of Palestine 1:250,000 map of 1946
(public domain in Israel and the UK; facts only are used, as for decision D-B in docs/oss/DECISIONS.md), using the scans
and georeferencing published by Palestine Open Maps (https://palopenmaps.org).

1949 armistice lines (content/map/armistice_lines_1949.geojson): digitised from the General Armistice Agreements of
1949 and their annexed maps (United Nations Treaty Series vol. 42; UN documents S/1264/Corr.1, S/1296, S/1302/Rev.1,
S/1353/Rev.1, and S/1471 with its signed 1950 map; UN documents are not copyrighted, ST/AI/189/Add.9/Rev.2), from the
UN Official Document System, UNISPAL and the UN Treaty Collection; the Egypt line uses the Survey of Palestine
1:100,000 sheet "Gaza" (Government of Palestine, decision D-B; National Library of Israel scan via Wikimedia Commons)
and the Lebanon line the sub-district data's Mandate frontier; town coordinates for georeferencing from Wikidata (CC0)
and Wikipedia. Decision D-A.

Portraits: public-domain and CC0 photographs from Wikimedia Commons; per-file records in ASSETS.portraits.yaml.

Fonts: EB Garamond, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (unity/Assets/UI/Fonts/OFL.txt).

